    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d419-a3">

                <pb facs="0565" n="495" sameAs="frus:frus1862/pg495"/>


                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.—Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <head>Mr. Perry to Consul
                        Barcena.</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Legation of the United
                            States</hi>,</placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1862-04-16"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >April</hi> 16, 1862.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p>Officially you cannot aid the shipwrecked Sumter’s men. From my private purse you
                    may expend fifty dollars in aid of those unfortunate persons.</p>
                <p>The letter of credit will go by the mail to-night.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>HORATIO J. PERRY.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Manuel Barcena y Franco</hi>, <hi
                            rendition="#italic">Consul of the United States at Vigo.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
